From b4af1443578b0a34dc89a419f3c1a298ef553950 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elliotttate <elliotttate@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:39:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 102/102] Aurora: in-between frames through draw-heavy scenes

The Forsaken Fortress draws 17,500 times a frame, and the translation worker
needed about 40 ms of each 33 ms game frame, 31 percent of it in the
in-between frame's blending. Most draws there (96 percent) repeat the vertex
constants of the draw before them. Those are now compared once, in
submit_draw_plan, instead of in the vertex uniform de-duplication, the
in-between pool and the in-between block's de-duplication; a draw that repeats
the one before and is matched the same way reuses its in-between block; and
the indexed position and normal matrices are blended only for draws that read
them (the others read only the current matrix). A Fortress-shaped load:
10.0 ms of blending a frame before, 1.8 ms after, with the same blended
values. frame_interp_test covers the reuse and the indexed matrices.
